    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "If $V=5\\pi r^2$ and $\\dfrac{dr}{dt}=2$, evaluate $\\dfrac{dV}{dt}$ correct to the nearest unit when $r=4.6$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$289$",
      "worked": "Variables: $V,r,t$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dV}{dt}&=\\frac{dV}{dr}\\times\\frac{dr}{dt}\\\\\\frac{dV}{dt}&=10\\pi r\\times2\\end{aligned}$$\nAt $r=4.6$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dV}{dt}&=10\\pi(4.6)\\times2\\\\\\frac{dV}{dt}&=92\\pi\\\\\\frac{dV}{dt}&\\approx289\\end{aligned}$$\nCorrect to the nearest unit.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 35
  },
